=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc15
diagnosis_text:
PC15 has a misconfigured default gateway. Its routing table points to `172.18.51.250` as the next-hop for all off-subnet traffic, while every other host in VLAN 51 (PC16, PC17, PC18) correctly uses `172.18.51.254`. The address `172.18.51.250` does not exist anywhere in the topology: PC15's own ARP cache shows it as permanently incomplete (hardware address `00:00:00:00:00:00`, Flags=0x0), and all pings to it return "Destination Host Unreachable" via ARP failure. By contrast, `172.18.51.254` resolves cleanly from PC15 and responds to ICMP, confirming it is the live inter-VLAN gateway.

The symptom pattern follows directly from this misconfiguration. Traffic from PC15 to `172.18.50.x` (Laptop4's wireless VLAN 50) is a different subnet, so the kernel must forward it via the default route. With the gateway address unresolvable, the kernel immediately emits an ICMP Host Unreachable back to PC15 — hence the reported failure. Traffic to VLAN 51 peers (PC16/17/18) is on-link and never consults the default route, so same-subnet reachability is unaffected, matching the user's observation that "PC15 can still ping its neighbors."

The fault is confined entirely to PC15's startup configuration. The corrective fix is to delete the bad route and install the correct one:
```
ip route del default via 172.18.51.250
ip route add default via 172.18.51.254
```
The startup script for pc15 must also be updated to replace `172.18.51.250` with `172.18.51.254` so the fix persists across restarts.
=== END ===